#: src/components/organisms/MatchmakingReport.re.mjs:826
#~ msgid ""
#~ "JP-style open play is the avoid-repeats baseline plus one intervention: a "
#~ "foursome is split when it is obviously lopsided — the pairs half a DUPR "
#~ "apart, the bar real organisers actually use. The surprise is that the "
#~ "intervention buys nothing measurable: JP lands within the error bars of "
#~ "its own baseline everywhere, a point or two of quality in this club at "
#~ "best. Splits that rare cannot move a session. Politeness that fixes only "
#~ "the egregious matches is worth almost nothing; the gains begin when every "
#~ "match is deliberately balanced, which is exactly what nobody does "
#~ "socially."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "日式開放打法是「避免重複」的基準做法，再加上一項介入：當一組四人明顯失衡時"
#~ "就拆開——兩對相差半個 DUPR，這正是實際主辦者採用的標準。令人意外的是，這項"
#~ "介入沒有帶來任何可衡量的效益：JP 在各處都落在自身基準的誤差範圍內，在這個"
#~ "球會頂多提升一兩點品質。如此罕見的拆分無法改變一場活動。只修正極端失衡的客"
#~ "套做法幾乎毫無價值；真正的收穫始於每一場對戰都被刻意平衡——而這正是社交場合"
#~ "中沒有人會做的事。"

